              <h3>Materials</h3>
              <p>Solid wood commands premium pricing; MDF and plywood offer durability at lower costs; laminate is the most budget-friendly option.</p>

              <h3>Labor</h3>
              <p>Pennsylvania professionals typically charge $50–$150 per hour, with installations taking 1–3 days depending on complexity.</p>

              <h3>Installation</h3>
              <p>Includes leveling, shimming, wall scribing, and toe-kick installation. Older Media, PA homes often require additional time due to uneven walls or floors.</p>

              <h3>Hardware</h3>
              <p>Full kitchens with 30 doors and drawers require $300–$1,500 in hardware depending on style and brand.</p>

              <h3>Customization</h3>
              <p>Features like pull-out shelves, spice racks, glass doors, and integrated lighting can add $500–$5,000+ to your total.</p>
