                    <tr><td>Size Options</td><td>Standard only</td><td>Any dimension</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Material Quality</td><td>Variable</td><td>Your choice</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Resale Value</td><td>Moderate</td><td>High</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Best For</td><td>Budget flips, rentals</td><td>Forever homes, luxury</td></tr>
                    <tr><td>Design Flexibility</td><td>Low</td><td>Unlimited</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Ways to Save -->
            <div class="post-body__section reveal">
              <h2>Ways to Save Money on Kitchen Cabinets</h2>
              <ul class="post-list">
                <li><strong>Cabinet refacing:</strong> Replace doors and drawer fronts while keeping existing boxes. Costs 40–60% less than full replacement.</li>
                <li><strong>Buy during sales:</strong> Major sales in January and July can save 20–30%.</li>
                <li><strong>Choose semi-custom over custom:</strong> Achieve 80% of the quality at 50% of the price.</li>
                <li><strong>Mix materials strategically:</strong> Use solid wood or glass fronts on upper cabinets; lower-cost materials on base cabinets.</li>
                <li><strong>Keep existing layout:</strong> Moving plumbing or electrical adds $1,000–$5,000+.</li>
                <li><strong>Order extra:</strong> Extra cabinet doors during the initial order cost far less than future reorders.</li>
              </ul>
